    "title": "What are Dollar General's Easter Hours?",
    "text": "Will Dollar General be open on Easter? Many people who are last-minute shoppers may be wondering this. For the past few years, many retailers have joined the trend and started closing on major holidays, allowing their employees to spend time with their families. This has become part of a retail blackout, in which some retailers are creating more family-friendly work conditions for their employes.Other retailers see days like Easter Sunday as an opportunity, especially since they know that other places will be closed that day. Therefore, they remain open to serve the general public. On which side of the retail spectrum does Dollar General stand?SIGN UP for the Dengarden / Parade Home & Garden newsletter for a weekly dose of our favorite house hacks, decor trends and shopping dealsIs Dollar General Open on Easter?It's good to know that if you need to shop for last-minute items like table settings, butter, milk, and extra pillows for unexpected guests, Dollar General will be open to meet your needs. Along with Dollar General, several retailers will be open that day. So, shoppers don't have to race in five minutes before the store closes Saturday night.Related: 3 Aldi Deal Finds Your Garden Can't Do Without This SpringThe only catch is that Dollar General, like other stores, may be operating on hours that aren't typical for a Sunday. Many are encouraged to check with their local Dollar General to find out their hours of operation.So, if you're so busy planning for Easter Sunday dinner that you forget the kids' Easter dye or the eggs to dip into the dye, Dollar General has your back. You can still save the day by picking some up on Sunday, just in time for the Easter egg hunt. Also, if you need to put together some cute Easter baskets, complete with candy and other essentials, they have the baskets and accessories to help you do so.Happy Easter!Related: These 5 Unique Items From Dolly Parton's Dollar General Collection Will Have You Shopping '9 to 5'",
